WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:03.203
Harry Kersh: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:04.671
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:07.040
between Pizza Hut in the UK and the US.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.575
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:13.480
Joe Avella: At a Pizza Hut in the US,

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.048
the pizza size that you want to get

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:17.317
is often dictated by the type
of crust you want to get.

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:18.685
For instance, this right here

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:21.321
is the smallest you can get, 6 inches,

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:23.223
but you can only get
it with the pan crust.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:25.692
Harry: In the UK, our
pizzas come in three sizes.

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:27.360
Firstly, we have the small.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.862
[crickets chirping]

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:29.896
OK, so they didn't actually

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:31.498
have a small pizza when we went,

00:00:31.498 --> 00:00:32.966
because they said that no one orders them

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:35.035
and if they do they normally
just give them mediums.

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:37.737
However, a small is supposed
to be 9 inches across.

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:37.771
Joe: In the US, at a Pizza Hut,

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:39.406
Joe: In the US, at a Pizza Hut,

00:00:39.406 --> 00:00:41.307
the only small pizza you can get

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:43.143
is one with gluten-free crust.

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:44.911
This one here is 10 inches.

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:46.146
Harry: The next size we have in the UK

00:00:46.146 --> 00:00:47.313
is the medium pizza.

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:49.582
This one is 11 inches across.

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:52.719
Joe: The large you also
get in the hand-tossed,

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:53.553
the pan,

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:55.188
or the thin and crispy crust.

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:56.623
This one: 14 inches.

00:00:58.291 --> 00:00:59.726
Harry: Pizza Hut in the UK also offers

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:01.361
an all-in-one pan box meal,

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:03.763
where you can get a large
pizza of your choice

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:06.032
as well as two sides and two sauces.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:07.033
Joe: Here in the US,

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:09.202
you can get two box meal options.

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:11.137
This first one is a medium pizza,

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:13.106
five breadsticks, and some dipping sauce,

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:16.943
and then 10 cinnamon
sticks with dipping icing.

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:18.511
And it comes in one box?

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:20.213
That really helps when you're eating this

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:21.714
in your car by yourself.

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:23.183
[laughing]

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:24.717
Not big enough, you say?

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:27.253
Don't worry. Pizza Hut has got
you and the family covered.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.689
This is the big dinner box.

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:31.691
Ooh, man!

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:33.760
[laughing] Look at this, dude!

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:36.496
It's like opening the
suitcase in "Pulp Fiction."

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:37.697
[angelic music]

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:39.432
This looks awesome!

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:40.967
You got two pizzas.

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:42.869
I got pepperoni, and I got sausage.

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:45.371
10 cheese sticks, and you get an option

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:47.974
of either pasta or chicken wings.

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:49.742
Get real. Get wings.

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:52.445
Joe: In the UK, we got these
ones from a restaurant,

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:54.781
and they gave us a portion
of six barbecue wings.

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:55.915
Joe: Not to be outdone,

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:58.718
we went ahead and proved a point to no one

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:00.353
by going just a little bit further

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:02.055
with our wing size options.

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:03.556
You can get six,

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:04.991
you can get 12,

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:06.392
you can get 18,

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:07.760
or 36.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:10.930
[upbeat tuba music]

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:13.900
Lemon pepper?

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.101
Nope, I don't like that.

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:18.738
Harry: Who's getting the
better deal for their money?

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:19.939
Well, in the UK,

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:23.776
a large cheese pizza will
cost you 15 pounds 99.

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:26.546
That's a price of 15
cents per square inch.

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:28.281
Joe: The US large hand-tossed cheese pizza

00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:29.816
is about $13.99,

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:32.285
which is about 9 cents per square inch,

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:34.554
making it about 40% cheaper

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:36.389
than the same pizza in the UK.

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:37.857
Harry: So, here we have

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:40.393
a large classic-crust cheese pizza

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:42.328
and a large pan-crust cheese pizza.

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:44.831
Now, these are the same
price and the same diameter.

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:45.665
We wanted to find out

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:47.133
which one gives you more
pizza for your money,

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:47.967
so what we're going to do

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:49.702
is try and weigh equivalent slices

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:51.671
and see which one comes out on top.

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:52.672
Joe: All right.

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:56.976
We will weigh a large slice ourselves.

00:02:56.976 --> 00:02:58.945
Harry: So, Pizza Hut
large pizzas in the UK

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:00.613
are supposed to be cut into 10 slices,

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:01.881
but they've actually cut this into eight,

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:03.516
so what we're going to do
is try and find the slices

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:06.085
that are the same size,
for scientific accuracy.

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:08.054
Let's weigh a slice of
classic crust cheese

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:09.689
and see what it comes to.

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:13.059
Now let's weigh the pan crust.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.332
So, our equivalent-size slice of pan pizza

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:20.733
is about 103 grams.

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:22.435
Joe: Similarly here in the US,

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:24.137
this is the hand-tossed, this is the pan,

00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:25.238
both large cheese.

00:03:25.238 --> 00:03:26.072
Pan.

00:03:29.142 --> 00:03:32.712
So, one slice of pan is about 125 grams.

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:33.279
Hm.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:34.881
Do the next one.

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:37.150
Slice is almost the exact same size.

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:38.184
80 grams.

00:03:38.184 --> 00:03:41.087
That's, like, significantly less pizza.

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:44.090
Same price. Ah, yeah. Stick with the pan.

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:46.125
Look how thick that is versus this.

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:50.463
Harry: In the UK, a large pan pizza

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:52.732
should be cut into 10
slices, but ours is eight.

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:54.133
Assuming it was 10 slices,

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:56.536
each slice would be 226 calories,

00:03:56.536 --> 00:03:58.304
and that brings the total for a large pan

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:00.406
to 2,260 calories.

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:02.742
Joe: In the US, our pizzas apparently

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:04.777
are all eight slices regardless of size,

00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:07.680
so one slice of a large
pan Pizza Hut pizza

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.649
is 360 calories,

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:13.853
making the entire pie 2,880 calories.

00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:16.222
Harry: One of these also
contains 99 grams of fat

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:19.158
as well as 3,400 milligrams of sodium.

00:04:22.128 --> 00:04:26.032
Joe: This entire pizza also
has about 135 grams of fat.

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:27.934
54 of those are saturated fat,

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:29.769
which I'm certain is the bad fat.

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:32.905
And it also has 5.31 grams of sodium.

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:34.073
That, in case you didn't know,

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:35.141
punch in,

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:39.779
is 221% of your daily sodium intake.

00:04:40.313 --> 00:04:41.881
Don't eat this all in one day.

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:44.250
Harry: It's got 100% of
your daily flavor in it.

00:04:46.686 --> 00:04:48.554
What about the most
calorific thing on the menu?

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:50.890
Well, in the UK, that's
a large stuffed crust

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.225
pepperoni feast.

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:56.162
If it is 10 slices, each
slice is 292 calories,

00:04:56.162 --> 00:04:59.098
bringing the total to 2,920.

00:04:59.332 --> 00:05:00.466
One of these pizzas contains

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:02.368
more than double your
daily sodium allowance

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:04.937
and more than triple your
saturated fat allowance.

00:05:04.971 --> 00:05:07.573
Joe: If you want to have even
more calories in your pizza,

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:10.443
then you've got to go with
the most calorific pizza

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:11.711
on the Pizza Hut menu,

00:05:11.711 --> 00:05:12.912
and, thank you, Conner,

00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:14.947
that is, of course, the meat lovers.

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:17.550
This entire thing is

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:20.453
3,760 calories.

00:05:20.453 --> 00:05:23.022
400% of your daily saturated fat.

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:24.457
400!

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:27.460
And it also is three
times your daily sodium.

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:29.495
If I've not put a fine enough point on it,

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:30.229
don't eat this.

00:05:31.731 --> 00:05:33.366
Harry: Here's everything
in a pan-pizza base

00:05:33.366 --> 00:05:34.400
from a UK Pizza Hut.

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:36.769
Wheat flour, water,

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:40.740
yeast (baker's yeast,
rehydrating agent E190),

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:43.142
vegetable rapeseed oil, salt,

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:46.312
premix (salt, calcium sulphate,

00:05:46.312 --> 00:05:48.481
emulsifiers E481,

00:05:48.481 --> 00:05:51.517
E472e, E471,

00:05:51.517 --> 00:05:53.953
flour-treatment agent E300,

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:56.756
enzyme (alpha amylase, xylanase,

00:05:56.756 --> 00:06:00.593
glucose oxidase, protease, cullulase)),

00:06:00.593 --> 00:06:03.963
sugar, flour-treatment
agent, ascorbic acid E300.

00:06:03.996 --> 00:06:06.899
Joe: In the US, our pan
dough has enriched flour,

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:08.368
which is bleached wheat flour,

00:06:08.368 --> 00:06:11.270
malted barley flour, niacin,

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:12.572
furious sulfate?

00:06:12.739 --> 00:06:14.273
Don't mess with that sulfate. He's pissed.

00:06:14.273 --> 00:06:16.576
Thiamine mononitrate, riboflavin,

00:06:16.576 --> 00:06:18.845
folic acid; water, yeast.

00:06:18.845 --> 00:06:22.382
It contains 2% or less
of salt, soybean oil,

00:06:22.382 --> 00:06:24.217
vital wheat gluten, sugar,

00:06:24.217 --> 00:06:25.852
enzymes, ascorbic acid,

00:06:25.852 --> 00:06:28.755
sodium stearoyl lass-ih-tight.

00:06:28.755 --> 00:06:30.656
Lac-the-lite.

00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:31.657
I think it's lac-the-lite.

00:06:31.958 --> 00:06:33.760
Harry: Now, the UK list
might actually look worse,

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:35.661
but you shouldn't be too
scared of the E numbers.

00:06:35.661 --> 00:06:37.597
For the most part, the
chemicals actually exist

00:06:37.597 --> 00:06:38.598
in the US dough as well

00:06:38.598 --> 00:06:40.666
but are referred to by different names.

00:06:40.666 --> 00:06:43.403
For example, E481 is just
another way of referring to

00:06:43.403 --> 00:06:45.204
the sodium stearoyl lactylate.

00:06:45.204 --> 00:06:48.241
Also, the E472e that's
found in the UK dough

00:06:48.241 --> 00:06:49.709
is otherwise known as datem,

00:06:49.709 --> 00:06:52.178
and that appears in the
US hand-tossed crust.

00:06:52.178 --> 00:06:53.513
What about the marinara sauce?

00:06:53.513 --> 00:06:56.048
Well, in the UK it contains tomatoes,

00:06:56.048 --> 00:06:58.584
citric acid, sugar, oregano,

00:06:58.584 --> 00:07:02.355
basil, marjoram, thyme,
salt, onion powder,

00:07:02.355 --> 00:07:06.058
maltodextrin, yeast extract,
rapeseed oil, guar gum,

00:07:06.058 --> 00:07:08.194
garlic powder, and silicone dioxide.

00:07:08.294 --> 00:07:10.263
Joe: Whereas our sauce
contains tomato puree,

00:07:10.263 --> 00:07:11.597
which is water and tomato paste,

00:07:11.597 --> 00:07:14.434
maltodextrin, salt, spices, garlic powder,

00:07:14.434 --> 00:07:16.969
tomato fibers, olive oil, canola oil,

00:07:16.969 --> 00:07:18.604
citric acid, and natural flavors,

00:07:18.604 --> 00:07:20.173
so it sounds like it's
pretty much the same thing.

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:21.541
Harry: How about the cheese?

00:07:21.541 --> 00:07:24.343
In the UK, we refer to
our cheese as mozzarella,

00:07:24.343 --> 00:07:25.711
and it contains the following:

00:07:25.711 --> 00:07:27.480
mozzarella cheese, salt,

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:29.449
lactic cultures, and potato starch.

00:07:29.715 --> 00:07:31.584
It's actually pretty short,
compared to the first two.

00:07:31.751 --> 00:07:33.820
Joe: In the US, the Pizza
Hut refers to its cheese

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:36.722
as cheese, which contains
mozzarella cheese,

00:07:36.722 --> 00:07:38.724
pasteurized milk, cheese cultures,

00:07:38.724 --> 00:07:41.227
salt, enzymes, modified food starch,

00:07:41.227 --> 00:07:44.297
sugarcane fiber, potassium chloride –

00:07:44.297 --> 00:07:45.131
[burps]

00:07:45.131 --> 00:07:46.232
Excuse me. Ugh!

00:07:46.466 --> 00:07:48.568
Natural flavors, ascorbic acid.

00:07:49.202 --> 00:07:49.769
Bleh!

00:07:50.303 --> 00:07:52.104
Harry: There is one thing
to look out for on the menu.

00:07:52.104 --> 00:07:53.940
If you're in the US and you get a salad,

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:56.976
the croutons contain
azodicarbonamide, or ADA.

00:07:56.976 --> 00:07:58.744
This is a substance that's
usually used to make

00:07:58.744 --> 00:08:01.948
vinyl foam plastics, which
form things like yoga mats.

00:08:01.948 --> 00:08:03.649
It's actually been banned from use in food

00:08:03.649 --> 00:08:05.585
in the UK since the 1990s.

00:08:05.751 --> 00:08:07.887
Joe: So, this is my comment
on the yoga-mat thing.

00:08:09.121 --> 00:08:10.056
It's always something.

00:08:10.056 --> 00:08:11.491
Even when we're trying to be healthy,

00:08:11.491 --> 00:08:13.392
our salad has yoga-mat plastic in it.

00:08:13.392 --> 00:08:14.427
It's ridiculous. Like,

00:08:14.427 --> 00:08:16.229
why do our croutons have plastic in them?

00:08:16.229 --> 00:08:17.997
Just get regular croutons without plastic!

00:08:17.997 --> 00:08:18.898
It doesn't make any sense.

00:08:21.434 --> 00:08:23.669
This pizza is the bomb,
dude. It's really good.

00:08:26.272 --> 00:08:27.974
Harry: Here is everything
you can only find on the menu

00:08:27.974 --> 00:08:29.141
at a UK Pizza Hut.

00:08:29.242 --> 00:08:30.610
And we've got quite a few exclusives!

00:08:30.776 --> 00:08:32.778
Joe: And these are all the
exclusives you can only get

00:08:32.778 --> 00:08:34.247
at a US Pizza Hut.

00:08:34.547 --> 00:08:36.048
Harry: So, I'm not sure if
it's like this in the US,

00:08:36.048 --> 00:08:37.783
but in the UK, Pizza Hut's operations

00:08:37.783 --> 00:08:39.352
are kind of split into two halves.

00:08:39.352 --> 00:08:40.786
You have a bunch of restaurants,

00:08:40.786 --> 00:08:42.555
where you will go and
have a sit-down meal,

00:08:42.555 --> 00:08:44.790
and then you also have a
bunch of carryout locations,

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.359
which just do delivery orders.

00:08:46.359 --> 00:08:47.660
The menus are actually slightly different,

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:49.195
depending on where you get your food from.

00:08:49.195 --> 00:08:51.631
The brown ones are actually
from a sit-down restaurant,

00:08:51.631 --> 00:08:53.633
and the red ones are from
a takeaway restaurant.

00:08:53.666 --> 00:08:54.934
We wanted to get a selection of both

00:08:54.934 --> 00:08:57.703
to see all of the foods you
can get from the UK Pizza Hut.

00:08:57.703 --> 00:09:00.072
Joe: Per what Harry was
talking about before,

00:09:00.072 --> 00:09:03.109
places for carryout versus delivery only,

00:09:03.109 --> 00:09:04.176
I have no idea.

00:09:04.176 --> 00:09:05.645
I just went on the website and ordered it,

00:09:05.645 --> 00:09:06.812
and this showed up, so.

00:09:07.079 --> 00:09:08.648
Harry: Let's start with
the exclusive pizzas.

00:09:08.648 --> 00:09:10.650
So, across these few
pizzas, we have pretty much

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:13.486
all of the exclusive
customizations available in the UK.

00:09:13.486 --> 00:09:14.921
We'll start with some of the doughs.

00:09:14.921 --> 00:09:16.923
On the left we have
our gluten-free option.

00:09:16.923 --> 00:09:18.591
I think there actually is
one of these in the US,

00:09:18.591 --> 00:09:20.293
but could be fun to compare.

00:09:20.293 --> 00:09:22.028
It looks pretty standard from the top.

00:09:22.028 --> 00:09:23.362
Then my personal favorite is here,

00:09:23.362 --> 00:09:25.097
which is the cheesy-bites crust.

00:09:25.097 --> 00:09:26.666
So, instead of just a standard crust,

00:09:26.666 --> 00:09:29.502
they get twists of dough
and fill them with cheese

00:09:29.502 --> 00:09:31.304
and then layer those around the outside.

00:09:31.304 --> 00:09:34.507
Here we have a sprinkled,
kind of, like, herby,

00:09:34.507 --> 00:09:36.709
cheesy situation on the crust.

00:09:36.709 --> 00:09:37.777
I've never had this one before.

00:09:37.777 --> 00:09:38.978
I think it's quite new.

00:09:38.978 --> 00:09:41.113
But it looks and smells pretty good.

00:09:41.113 --> 00:09:43.616
And then finally we have a
vegan stuffed-crust option,

00:09:43.616 --> 00:09:45.351
which is great because you shouldn't

00:09:45.351 --> 00:09:48.387
be robbed of extra cheese
just for being vegan.

00:09:48.521 --> 00:09:50.323
Joe: Right in the center here

00:09:50.323 --> 00:09:54.327
is the US exclusive Pizza Hut pizza.

00:09:55.094 --> 00:09:56.495
It's shaped like a heart,

00:09:56.495 --> 00:09:59.098
and it has all the ingredients
you only get in the US.

00:09:59.098 --> 00:10:03.336
Went with the creamy garlic
Parmesan base, as a sauce.

00:10:03.336 --> 00:10:05.771
The crust is a flavored crust,

00:10:05.771 --> 00:10:07.239
and I went with the Hut Favorite.

00:10:07.239 --> 00:10:08.441
I have no idea what that is.

00:10:08.441 --> 00:10:09.976
And exclusive meats I had put on here

00:10:09.976 --> 00:10:13.012
was Italian sausage, meatballs, and pork.

00:10:13.012 --> 00:10:15.915
Also has banana peppers.

00:10:16.148 --> 00:10:17.183
Shaped like a heart.

00:10:17.183 --> 00:10:18.618
Why it's all year round

00:10:18.618 --> 00:10:20.886
and not just on Valentine's
Day is beyond me,

00:10:20.886 --> 00:10:22.154
but apparently you can do this.

00:10:22.154 --> 00:10:25.291
Harry: Nothing says romance
like a heart-shaped pizza.

00:10:25.291 --> 00:10:26.392
How do you cut that thing, though?

00:10:26.392 --> 00:10:27.727
It seems like getting even slices

00:10:27.727 --> 00:10:29.395
out of that would be
an absolute nightmare.

00:10:29.795 --> 00:10:31.097
Joe: Look what I brought.

00:10:31.097 --> 00:10:33.566
All right, so I guess I will just do...

00:10:34.567 --> 00:10:36.469
[slicing]
[jazzy music]

00:10:36.469 --> 00:10:37.937
Right?

00:10:48.547 --> 00:10:49.915
Yeah, no, I hate that.

00:10:50.016 --> 00:10:52.218
Harry: Now, as is becoming
traditional on "Food Wars,"

00:10:52.218 --> 00:10:55.121
what we have here is a UK Only pizza.

00:10:55.121 --> 00:10:58.157
This is a pizza with
the cheesy bites crust,

00:10:58.157 --> 00:11:01.060
with vegan pepperphoni,
caramelized onions,

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:02.294
and rocket on it.

00:11:06.232 --> 00:11:07.433
It's actually not bad.

00:11:07.433 --> 00:11:08.701
I'm going to try a cheesy bite as well,

00:11:08.701 --> 00:11:10.403
because I feel that's
part of the experience.

00:11:13.572 --> 00:11:16.709
I think this is the first
UK Only creation we've made

00:11:16.709 --> 00:11:18.044
that I can actually endorse.

00:11:18.044 --> 00:11:19.578
This is actually pretty good.

00:11:20.079 --> 00:11:23.049
The vegan pepperoni, I've
got to say, is actually good.

00:11:23.049 --> 00:11:24.717
The texture is pretty much there.

00:11:24.717 --> 00:11:26.052
It's quite salty,

00:11:26.052 --> 00:11:27.687
a little bit of spice to it,

00:11:27.687 --> 00:11:29.055
and the cheesy bites,

00:11:29.055 --> 00:11:31.157
it does make it a little
bit harder to hold,

00:11:31.157 --> 00:11:32.258
'cause it's like,

00:11:32.258 --> 00:11:33.826
what are you supposed to hold on to?

00:11:33.826 --> 00:11:36.796
But they themselves are
actually really tasty.

00:11:36.896 --> 00:11:39.065
So, yeah. Thumbs-up for the UK Only.

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:42.968
Joe: Pizza Hut's most infamous menu item

00:11:42.968 --> 00:11:46.439
is their take on the
calzone, aka the P'Zone.

00:11:46.439 --> 00:11:49.208
P, apostrophe, Z, O, N, E.

00:11:49.208 --> 00:11:50.609
I have had a P'Zone before.

00:11:50.609 --> 00:11:51.811
They're actually really good.

00:11:51.811 --> 00:11:54.447
I was really bummed to find out that

00:11:54.447 --> 00:11:56.615
where we are filming it, in
this part of the United States,

00:11:56.615 --> 00:11:58.984
the Los Angeles, California, area,

00:11:58.984 --> 00:11:59.018
Went on the internet,

00:11:59.018 --> 00:12:02.021
unfortunately, the P'Zone is not available.

00:12:02.021 --> 00:12:02.755
Went on the internet,

00:12:02.755 --> 00:12:04.724
and sure enough the P'Zone is available,

00:12:04.724 --> 00:12:07.560
at least in Saint Louis
and at least in Cincinnati,

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:08.928
so if anyone watching in the United States

00:12:08.928 --> 00:12:11.097
would like to ship me a P'Zone

00:12:11.097 --> 00:12:12.965
from their P'Zone-plentiful part

00:12:12.965 --> 00:12:14.967
of the United States, please do.

00:12:14.967 --> 00:12:16.135
Um,

00:12:16.135 --> 00:12:17.570
I don't know how I'd get you my address.

00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:18.237
[laughs]

00:12:18.671 --> 00:12:19.505
Harry: Now, as you can see,

00:12:19.505 --> 00:12:21.674
we have a bunch of
exclusive sides in the UK.

00:12:21.674 --> 00:12:23.576
I'm not entirely sure
what all of these are,

00:12:23.576 --> 00:12:25.044
because some of them look very similar,

00:12:25.044 --> 00:12:26.045
so we'll have a run-through

00:12:26.045 --> 00:12:28.147
and I'll try and point out
the ones I can identify.

00:12:28.214 --> 00:12:30.716
So, at the back here, we've
got some potato wedges.

00:12:30.716 --> 00:12:33.319
I'm never really sure why
restaurants offer potato wedges,

00:12:33.319 --> 00:12:35.054
because to me they're
just worse than fries

00:12:35.054 --> 00:12:36.222
in pretty much every metric.

00:12:36.222 --> 00:12:38.157
Then we've got a bunch of
different chicken options.

00:12:38.157 --> 00:12:41.227
We've got these chicken-strip things here,

00:12:41.227 --> 00:12:45.364
we've got these
spicy-looking nugget things,

00:12:45.364 --> 00:12:48.968
we've got these
herby-looking nugget things,

00:12:48.968 --> 00:12:52.404
and then we've got some
plain-looking nugget things,

00:12:52.404 --> 00:12:55.641
as well as these, I think,
Southern fried bites.

00:12:55.641 --> 00:12:57.710
Apologies to actual Southern Americans,

00:12:57.710 --> 00:12:59.712
because I'm sure they are an abomination.

00:12:59.879 --> 00:13:02.448
Joe: Here in America, we have
something called WingStreet.

00:13:02.448 --> 00:13:05.351
From what I understand, WingStreet
was a separate business,

00:13:05.351 --> 00:13:06.719
or a separate restaurant chain,

00:13:06.719 --> 00:13:07.920
that is owned by the same brand,

00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:10.623
and therefore you can get WingStreet wings

00:13:10.623 --> 00:13:12.091
when you order from Pizza Hut.

00:13:12.091 --> 00:13:13.926
Anyway, we have a bunch of
different sauce options,

00:13:13.926 --> 00:13:16.562
like we have a honey barbecue,

00:13:16.562 --> 00:13:20.099
Buffalo, which can be mild
or medium or burning hot,

00:13:20.099 --> 00:13:22.835
garlic Parmesan, and, of course...

00:13:22.835 --> 00:13:24.370
what was this one that I hate?

00:13:24.370 --> 00:13:25.204
Conner: Lemon pepper.

00:13:25.204 --> 00:13:26.572
Joe: Lemon pepper, which I don't like.

00:13:26.572 --> 00:13:29.775
You can also get a Hawaiian
teriyaki, a spicy garlic,

00:13:29.775 --> 00:13:31.644
a Cajun-style dry rub,

00:13:31.644 --> 00:13:33.946
or you can just get these bad boys naked.

00:13:33.946 --> 00:13:36.282
Oof! Worst time to burp there.

00:13:36.916 --> 00:13:38.050
Harry: Why do all the
WingStreet containers

00:13:38.050 --> 00:13:39.018
look like Death Stars?

00:13:39.018 --> 00:13:42.121
That seems like a suboptimal
way to transport your food.

00:13:42.121 --> 00:13:43.389
It's like a half-bowl,

00:13:43.389 --> 00:13:44.824
and the lid is like another bowl.

00:13:44.924 --> 00:13:46.225
Joe: Sauce talk.

00:13:46.325 --> 00:13:47.860
Deep voice: Sauce talk!

00:13:47.927 --> 00:13:50.129
Joe: You can also get
exclusive sauces on the side,

00:13:50.129 --> 00:13:52.464
for instance, blue cheese.

00:13:52.464 --> 00:13:53.966
You can get yourself some ranch,

00:13:53.966 --> 00:13:55.935
a cup of marinara,

00:13:55.935 --> 00:13:58.938
and the Buffalo sauces
of various temperatures,

00:13:58.938 --> 00:13:59.972
honey barbecue sauce.

00:13:59.972 --> 00:14:01.774
Sides of sauces. We've got you covered.

00:14:02.041 --> 00:14:05.211
Harry: Outside of that,
we've got some nachos.

00:14:05.311 --> 00:14:07.046
We've also got these cheesy bites,

00:14:07.046 --> 00:14:09.081
which are just triangles of cheese

00:14:09.081 --> 00:14:10.983
that get breaded and deep-fried,

00:14:10.983 --> 00:14:13.586
because I guess cholesterol
isn't a thing anymore.

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:16.155
We've also got some onion rings,

00:14:16.155 --> 00:14:18.257
we've got some corncobs,

00:14:18.257 --> 00:14:20.426
we have cheesy garlic bread,

00:14:20.426 --> 00:14:21.827
regular garlic bread,

00:14:21.827 --> 00:14:24.997
and we also have mac 'n' cheese,

00:14:24.997 --> 00:14:26.332
but it turns out...

00:14:27.433 --> 00:14:29.235
you can also do that with mac 'n' cheese.

00:14:29.635 --> 00:14:31.871
Joe: Also, WingStreet fries,

00:14:31.871 --> 00:14:34.240
just orders of fries that
it looks like you can get

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:37.176
pretty much the same flavors as the wings.

00:14:37.176 --> 00:14:38.644
I'm going to toss them in the same sauce.

00:14:38.644 --> 00:14:39.745
Here's a lemon pepper.

00:14:39.745 --> 00:14:41.447
Ugh, not as good.

00:14:41.447 --> 00:14:43.549
I don't like lemon
pepper, I'm finding out.

00:14:43.549 --> 00:14:45.484
Something I thought every
Pizza Hut around the world had,

00:14:45.484 --> 00:14:47.453
apparently not, are breadsticks.

00:14:47.453 --> 00:14:48.854
Looks like five sticks.

00:14:48.854 --> 00:14:50.656
Harry: Joe, we went over this
in the Papa John's episode.

00:14:50.656 --> 00:14:51.757
That is not a breadstick.

00:14:51.757 --> 00:14:54.093
Joe: And you can also get cheesy bread,

00:14:54.093 --> 00:14:55.828
which is like breadsticks,

00:14:55.828 --> 00:14:58.364
but they bake them with
cheese on top of them.

00:14:58.364 --> 00:15:00.099
This is the chicken Alfredo.

00:15:00.099 --> 00:15:01.100
[laughs]

00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:02.534
Is this just how they packed it?

00:15:02.534 --> 00:15:04.270
There's a Buffalo sauce

00:15:04.270 --> 00:15:07.006
and a barbecue sauce in here. Why?

00:15:07.006 --> 00:15:08.474
These guys right here,

00:15:08.474 --> 00:15:10.209
I'm probably going to
pronounce them wrong.

00:15:10.209 --> 00:15:12.845
Quepapas. Like tater tots?

00:15:13.512 --> 00:15:14.146
Yeah!

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:16.215
Harry: We also have a
bunch of exclusive desserts

00:15:16.215 --> 00:15:17.383
at UK Pizza Huts.

00:15:17.383 --> 00:15:19.218
If you're eating at a restaurant,
you have a few options,

00:15:19.218 --> 00:15:21.387
including one of these brownie slices.

00:15:21.654 --> 00:15:23.889
This is actually a vegan
vanilla cheesecake,

00:15:23.889 --> 00:15:27.226
which looks and smells
really good, I've got to say.

00:15:27.226 --> 00:15:29.495
And then you have a cookie-dough thing,

00:15:29.495 --> 00:15:30.529
which usually comes with

00:15:30.529 --> 00:15:32.131
a little scoop of ice cream as well.

00:15:32.131 --> 00:15:35.234
Joe: And the desserts. Huh!

00:15:35.234 --> 00:15:36.969
We're almost done, people.

00:15:36.969 --> 00:15:38.504
The thing right in front of me

00:15:38.504 --> 00:15:40.940
are Cinnabon mini buns.

00:15:40.973 --> 00:15:44.310
This is the Ultimate Hershey's
chocolate chip cookie.

00:15:44.710 --> 00:15:46.445
Harry: If you're getting delivery
from Pizza Hut in the UK,

00:15:46.445 --> 00:15:48.147
there are also some exclusive options.

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:51.250
This is another sort of
giant-cookie-dough situation.

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:53.052
Bites of Ben &amp; Jerry's cookie dough.

00:15:53.052 --> 00:15:54.520
Again, it's usually served frozen,

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:56.689
but they've now unfortunately defrosted.

00:15:56.689 --> 00:15:58.691
And then they have some
branded ice creams as well.

00:15:59.158 --> 00:16:02.528
Joe: We've got their
triple chocolate brownie.

00:16:02.528 --> 00:16:03.829
Last but not least.

00:16:03.829 --> 00:16:06.165
Cinnamon sticks with a lot of icing.

00:16:06.532 --> 00:16:08.167
You know I gotta do it.

00:16:08.167 --> 00:16:10.736
[upbeat string music]

00:16:15.107 --> 00:16:17.076
[Joe sighs]

00:16:17.977 --> 00:16:19.445
Harry: See, I always
think that these look like

00:16:19.445 --> 00:16:21.313
little tables for mice.

00:16:21.313 --> 00:16:24.450
So you could just put the
tiny slice on the tiny table.

00:16:24.450 --> 00:16:25.284
[laughs]

00:16:25.284 --> 00:16:27.386
And have a little mouse dinner party.

